    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d439">

                <pb facs="0447" n="435" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg435"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.49 Refugees/2397: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in the Dominican Republic</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Scotten</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ciudad Trujillo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-01-31T11:00:00-05:00">January 31,
                            1941—11 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 31—12:42 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>20. From Pell. The meeting<anchor n="4" xml:id="d439-f1"/> took place without
                    incident after Barois agreed to hand a memorandum of the plan described in
                    Legation’s telegram No. 18, January 29, 1 p.m., to the Secretary of the
                    Intergovernmental Committee<anchor n="5" xml:id="d439-f2"/> for reference as to
                    distribution to the Chairman.<anchor n="6" xml:id="d439-f3"/> [Pell.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Scotten</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d439-f1" n="4" xml:id="d439-f1-content">
                <p>The meeting was held January 30 through February 3, 1941; <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Report on the Meeting of the Intergovernmental Committee at Ciudad Trujillo
                        and the Sosua Settlement in the Dominican Republic</hi>, dated February 28,
                    1941. (840.48 Refugees/2585).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d439-f2" n="5" xml:id="d439-f2-content">
                <p>Alfred Wagg.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d439-f3" n="6" xml:id="d439-f3-content">
                <p>The Earl of Winterton.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
